### Try Alt+T

Place your cursor anywhere in this file and press `Alt+T`. The
QuickPick lists every tag (including implicit parents like `project`
and `inventory/homelab`). Pick one → Search Editor opens with results
pre-populated.

**Keybinding caveats.** `Alt+T` follows the same convention as the
other Alt-letter bindings — gated to `editorLangId == 'tsk' &&
editorTextFocus`, so it only fires when you're inside a `.tsk`
editor. Third-party extensions with an equally specific `when` clause
could shadow it; some EU keyboard layouts (where `Alt+letter` produces
a typed character) may need a rebind via Keyboard Shortcuts.

## Parser model (M2)

The parser reads every line above into a `Task` record exposing `marker`,
`indent`, `content`, an insertion-ordered `metadata` Map, a `tags` array, and
a zero-indexed `line`. Nothing visible yet — M3 plugs this into a SQLite cache
and surfaces it via commands — but the model is exercised by these examples.

